  "problem": "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},\u2026,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,2].$ If $\u0394{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})\u0394{z}_{k}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We can simplify the given summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})\u0394{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})\u0394{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})\u0394{z}_{2}+\u22ef+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})\u0394{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+\u22ef+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+\u22ef+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+\u22ef+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})\u0394{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
